// A body ending in an expression is how a function returns one, but
// only where the signature says something comes back.  Here it says
// nothing, so the 1 is not a return value and what it computes goes
// nowhere -- a value nothing reads, which is refused wherever it
// stands.  Naming a return type is what would hand it back.
fn f():
    1

@start
fn main():
    _ ← 1
